-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS (read end-to-end before writing native code)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PlaybackSpeedMenu is a compact, **stateless controlled** control (59 lines). Props:
  • speed: ReplaySpeed                       — the current scrub speed (parent-owned)
  • onChange: (ReplaySpeed) => void          — notifies the parent of the next value
  • className?: string                       — optional style override
Only hook: useTranslation (the P1/S10 localisation facade). There is NO data fetch — no
useQuery/useEffect/fetch — so the control has NO async data lifecycle.

Module exports reproduced verbatim:
  • REPLAY_SPEEDS: ReplaySpeed[] = [1, 10, 25, 50, 100]
  • shiftSpeed(current, delta)  — step by `delta` slots, CLAMPED to the ends
                                  (unknown current → slot 0, web `idx === -1 ? 0 : idx`)
  • nextSpeed(current)          — cycle to the next-fastest, WRAPS (web `(idx + 1) % length`)
Composition / interaction:
  • <Button variant="ghost" size="sm" className="… text-xs font-mono"> showing `{speed}x`
    and a <ChevronDown class="opacity-50"/>.
  • onClick      → onChange(nextSpeed(speed))      (forward, wrap)
  • onContextMenu→ onChange(shiftSpeed(speed,-1))  (one slower, clamp; preventDefault)
  • aria-label   → t('replay.controls.speed', 'Playback speed')   ← the ONLY i18n key

STATES — honest mapping (Covenant #1 / #2 / #5): the generic per-surface template lists
loading / empty / error / stale / offline. The web source has NO data source (only `speed`
+ `onChange` + `useTranslation`), so those async-data states DO NOT EXIST in the source and
are intentionally NOT fabricated. Every branch that genuinely exists IS reproduced + tested:
  • each of the 5 speed values renders (1x / 10x / 25x / 50x / 100x)
  • forward cycle advances through each slot and WRAPS 100x → 1x
  • backward step goes one slower and CLAMPS at 1x (+ multi-slot jumps, 0-delta identity)
  • the current speed is checkmarked in the menu (the selected-row affordance)

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NATIVE DESIGN (Apple HIG — SwiftUI, iOS 18 / iPadOS 18 / macOS 15)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
• Control: SwiftUI `Menu(content:label:primaryAction:)` — the HIG-idiomatic counterpart of the
  web cycling button + secondary gesture:
    - primaryAction = model.cycleForward(from: speed)   ⟷ web onClick (tap cycles forward, wraps)
    - menu open (long-press on iOS / right-click on macOS) ⟷ web onContextMenu (secondary gesture);
      content lists every speed for direct selection — a faithful SUPERSET of the web "one slower"
      step, with the current speed checkmarked. cycleBackward()/shiftSpeed(-1) is preserved as a
      first-class, unit-tested model method (the verbatim port of the web onContextMenu handler).
• Label: `{speed}x` in the small body face with `.monospacedDigit()` (the parity of web `text-xs
  font-mono` — stable digit width across 1→10→25→50→100). The web lucide `ChevronDown` maps to the
  native `Menu` disclosure indicator (HIG-idiomatic), so the label stays text-only.
• Controlled: `speed` is supplied by the parent on every render (exactly like the web source); the
  view is a pure function of it. The model owns only the `onChange` callback + telemetry.
• Tokens only (P1/S9): Color.TS.{textPrimary,surfaceGlass,bg}, Font.TS.{bodySm,panel},
  TSSpacing.{xs,sm,md}, TSRadius.{sm,md}. No Tailwind ports, no raw hex, no ad-hoc typography.
• Binding (P1/S8): no HTTP from the view; the only "data source" (useTranslation) is the P1/S10
  facade. The @MainActor @Observable PlaybackSpeedMenuModel carries the onChange notification +
  the once-only view.opened emission off the view.
• Accessibility: .accessibilityLabel("Playback speed") + .accessibilityValue("{speed}x") on the
  control (VoiceOver: "Playback speed, 10x, pop-up button"); each menu row labelled "{n}x" and the
  current row carries .isSelected. Dynamic Type via system text styles; no motion added (reduce-
  motion safe). Min targets iOS 18 / macOS 15.
• Telemetry (P1/S11): emits `view.opened` with surface slug "PlaybackSpeedMenu" exactly once on
  first appearance, via a testable diagnostics seam (OSLog default; injectable adapter).

NOTE — scope: the atomic component-library control `TSPlaybackSpeedMenu` in
Sources/Components/DataDisplay/Playback.swift (a generic [0.5,1,2,4] Double picker) is OUT OF SCOPE
